d3d11: upscale a picture smaller than its window with MetalFX

A program that renders smaller than its window (a lower resolution chosen in a game, or any
program while Wine's Retina mode is off) had its picture stretched to the window by the window
server, which blurs it. Every swap chain is now the kind that can upscale with MetalFX's
spatial scaler, and does so whenever its buffers are between 5% and 4x smaller than the window
is in display pixels, in both directions: the picture is upscaled to exactly the window's
pixels. A program that upscales by itself (DLSS and the like) hands over a picture of the
window's size already and is left alone, as are multisampled swap chains. The window's size is
looked at again every 30 frames, since a window can change size without its buffers being
resized. DXMT_METALFX_SPATIAL_SWAPCHAIN=1 still gives the fixed factor it always did;
FINEWINE_METALFX_AUTO=0 turns the automatic upscaling off.

The Metal bridge reports a layer's size in display pixels for this (two fields at the end of
WMTLayerProps, filled in by getProps).

